# App Promotion Website — Permanent Development Rules

## Technology

This project uses:

- HTML5
- CSS3
- Vanilla JavaScript

Do NOT introduce:

- React
- Vue
- Angular
- Next.js
- Bootstrap
- Tailwind
- jQuery
- unnecessary frontend libraries

unless explicitly requested.

## Project philosophy

This is a static, SEO-friendly app promotion/discovery website.

The developer already knows HTML, CSS and JavaScript.

Therefore:

- Keep code readable.
- Keep code easy to manually edit.
- Avoid unnecessary abstraction.
- Avoid unnecessary complexity.
- Use meaningful class names.
- Keep CSS organized.
- Keep JavaScript modular and understandable.

## SEO

SEO is a major requirement.

Important content must exist in HTML.

Do NOT make the entire website dependent on JavaScript-generated content.

Important:

- headings
- app names
- descriptions
- navigation links
- category links
- app detail links
- primary page content

should be available in HTML.

JavaScript should primarily enhance the experience.

## Reference screenshots

The supplied screenshots are design references only.

Do not clone them.

Do not copy their source code.

Do not copy their branding, text, images or exact visual identity.

Use them to understand:

- visual hierarchy
- card composition
- spacing
- backgrounds
- responsive behavior
- presentation style

Main1 and Main-res are the primary visual references.

cardref and cardref-res are primarily references for the concept of displaying trending/featured apps.

## Responsive design

Mobile is not simply a smaller desktop version.

Components should be intentionally redesigned for mobile where necessary.

Pay special attention to:

- featured cards
- navigation
- hero
- app grids
- buttons
- typography
- spacing

## Maintainability

Use CSS variables for:

- colors
- spacing where appropriate
- border radius
- shadows
- typography values where useful

Do not scatter repeated values throughout the stylesheet.

## Important content

Do not invent:

- fake ratings
- fake reviews
- fake download numbers
- fake security claims
- fake companies
- fake awards
- fake user counts

Use clearly marked placeholders when real information is not available.

## Modification safety

When working on a specific feature:

- inspect the existing implementation first
- modify only the relevant files
- do not unnecessarily rewrite unrelated sections
- preserve existing functionality
- preserve existing SEO
- preserve responsive behavior
- avoid breaking previously completed sections

Before finishing a task, check for:

- console errors
- broken links
- layout overflow
- obvious responsive issues
- accidental CSS conflicts

## Phase 5 — Featured / trending cards (DEFERRED)

Phase 5 is the three ranked featured/trending app cards on the homepage
(`#trending`, between the hero and the app directory).

Status: **deferred**. Do not implement it until the user explicitly says
to implement Phase 5.

Do not:

- build those cards, a simplified stand-in, or dummy app data
- populate `#trending` / `.phase-reserved`
- write JavaScript whose job is to generate the missing cards
- remove, relocate, or reuse that reserved section for another feature

If a later phase genuinely cannot proceed without those cards, ask before
implementing the dependency. Independent work (directory, categories,
detail pages, search on existing UI, SEO, a11y, performance) may continue.